# Agent onboarding (PAIR monorepo)

Before writing or changing code in this repo, read its rules and docs into
context and follow them:

- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — the always-on architecture and discipline rules,
  especially `architecture.mdc` (boundaries, ownership, reactive state) and
  `service-contracts.mdc` (desktop ↔ services contract checks).
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — workflow, build, and contribution conventions.
- The relevant `docs/*` for the area you are touching (e.g.
  `docs/building.md`, `desktop/docs/architecture.md`,
  `desktop/docs/services-backend.md`, `desktop/docs/services-parity.md`).
- `.agents/skills/*` when a matching skill exists (e.g. `kaizen-ui`,
  `sync-backend`).

`services/` is the backend source of truth in this monorepo; `desktop/` is the
Electron UI. PAIR relays cluster/engine commands and renders backend state — it
does not reimplement backend services in TypeScript.
